ine kind of benefits me  in a way because i  like am able to express myself when i  have like a small group of people  around me and people that i actually am  close with rather than like a huge  like team so save your best excuses  they can't get me through this  why were people upset that you they said  that you were like copying madison beer  which i know madison i've interviewed  her you guys are both such  different and lovely people  but how did that make you feel is there  anything else that you just want to say  about that matter  well um i did not copy her um  it kind of hurt when people said that  because my  song was so emotional  and so personal to me that when people  said that i was copying her song in her  music video it  really like kind of took away from my  feelings and what i went through  and the whole meaning behind the song we  did use rain  um both in our music videos but i think  mine this like what it symbolized for me  was way different i kind of want to show  like the endless amount of tears that i  cried during the time that i wrote the  song  and like there would be times where i  just like sit in the shower and like  ball up and just cry  and in the music video i'm just sitting  like like balling up and just letting  rainfall on me so i kind of wanted to  resemble that  um but in no means would i ever want to  copy her especially for my first song  i wouldn't want to be known for that but  um  yeah well thank you for setting the  record straight on that and i'm sorry  once again that people  like to just ruin things sometimes  not frustrating but one day we're all  going to learn it's way better to spread  love than it is to spread hate and i  hope that if anything from this  interview that's what people take away  [Music]  you said music was always the goal like  when did you first realize that you were  musical  or that you could sing and write yeah  i've been singing and writing since i  could talk  so yeah how many songs do you feel